From 70aaee024873a0d5587ccd1503400828f84cd933 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 19:40:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add one-time backfill for pre-pipeline experience
 translations
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

syncExperienceTranslations/syncSectionTranslations/syncFactTranslations
(translateExperience.ts) only fire on admin save, via /api/translate-
experience. Any experience_content/experience_sections/experience_facts
row created (or last saved) before that pipeline existed has no row in
its *_translations table, so the proposal page silently falls back to
English for it — visible on the proposal page today (facts like
"Boat"/"Availability", experience title/description, etc. still in
English for several experiences).

backfill-experience-translations.mjs re-implements the same hash/upsert
logic as translateExperience.ts (can't import the .ts module from a
plain node script) and loops over all three tables, translating only
rows missing an "ok" translation for the current English hash — safe
to re-run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
